      "normalized_sha256": "993f1ddeb82f8ec3058462bbc0bc6a359326253665e58baa0229c8ff3387f51e",
      "rationale": "Base equation defining the structural helper tailIS on the empty IntSeq; it introduces the named proof term's empty case rather than asserting an independent fact about program execution.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-993f1ddeb82f8ec3058462bbc0bc6a359326253665e58baa0229c8ff3387f51e",
      "start_line": 11,
      "text": "  rule tailIS(.IntSeq) => .IntSeq"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 12,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "76f74f31823745350d94934f77a8b1740fb37bf6ce4be8986b32cd0e40ea55d6",
      "rationale": "Constructor equation defining tailIS on a nonempty IntSeq by selecting its tail; together with the empty case it is the structural definition of the helper.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-76f74f31823745350d94934f77a8b1740fb37bf6ce4be8986b32cd0e40ea55d6",
      "start_line": 12,
      "text": "  rule tailIS(iCons(_:Int, CS:IntSeq)) => CS"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 16,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "7d8832f9476a30d90c0dc5ff351d655f77be7e3f7d280223e5275d3f137e948f",
      "rationale": "Guarded defining equation for overlapCount when the pattern is empty, assigning the boundary-count branch of the mathematical summary.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-7d8832f9476a30d90c0dc5ff351d655f77be7e3f7d280223e5275d3f137e948f",
      "start_line": 14,
      "text": "  rule overlapCount(S:IntSeq, P:IntSeq)\n    => isLen(S) +Int 1\n    requires P ==K .IntSeq"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 20,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "29f9efb6fc47c221fe5c4d6a8b72995b4966c7b257bd75c9928ce9d7ccbf0a9b",
      "rationale": "Guarded base equation for overlapCount on an empty source and a nonempty pattern; it is one disjoint case of the summary definition.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-29f9efb6fc47c221fe5c4d6a8b72995b4966c7b257bd75c9928ce9d7ccbf0a9b",
      "start_line": 18,
      "text": "  rule overlapCount(.IntSeq, P:IntSeq)\n    => 0\n    requires notBool (P ==K .IntSeq)"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 27,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "48a4b84d7a4f49eddd82fbf489ed5db68e8505668dbff98cd6bb049cbb651062",
      "rationale": "Guarded recursive equation defining overlapCount for nonempty source and pattern values by testing the current prefix and recurring on tailIS.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-48a4b84d7a4f49eddd82fbf489ed5db68e8505668dbff98cd6bb049cbb651062",
      "start_line": 22,
      "text": "  rule overlapCount(S:IntSeq, P:IntSeq)\n    => (#if startsWith(P, S)\n        #then 1 #else 0 #fi)\n       +Int overlapCount(tailIS(S), P)\n    requires notBool (S ==K .IntSeq)\n     andBool notBool (P ==K .IntSeq)"
    }
  ],
